4. Assess demand vs channel stuffing: For each of the top-3 combos, compute supporting signals from the CSV: (a) return rate trend in the 3 months before and after the spike month, (b) whether the spike is a single-month spike or sustained, (c) compare the spike month's volume to the next month's volume. Save a structured assessment table to offline_data/stuffing_assessment.csv → code_agent
5. Write Markdown report with embedded data: Write a comprehensive Markdown report to offline_data/volume_anomaly_report.md. Requirements: (1) H1 title; (2) at least one data table showing the top-3 combos with their ratio, month, and return rate; (3) every key number must carry an inline source annotation in the format '（来源：offline_data/regional_sales.csv 的 <列名>，<聚合口径与样本行数>）' or '（来源：由前述两行计算）'; (4) a concluding paragraph judging whether each spike is more likely real demand or channel stuffing, with reasoning; (5) all conclusions derived solely from the local CSV. → code_agent
